{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"state-mutation-round-3-follow-ups","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State mutation round 3 follow-ups"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Base revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cfb03f201"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" after #2032 and #2033)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This record closes the four items that the round 3 record and the\nready-callback truncate record left open. One is a bug fix. The cache delete\nstays, with witnesses. #2030 on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" made the other two unnecessary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-metadata-rebuild-after-a-canceled-earlier-transaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Metadata rebuild after a canceled earlier transaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gap."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The round 3 record called RB2, a mutant that keeps stale automatic\nmetadata writes through a rebuild, equivalent within legal histories. Reaching\nit needed a canceled earlier transaction, which the grammar did not generate."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Correction, 2026-10-06."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The outcome below is wrong. A transaction begun\ninside an open one can still commit first, and the rebuild then reclassifies\nthe open one's inserts. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" loses last-write-wins there. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"2026-10-06-nested-begin-metadata-rebuild.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2026-10-06-nested-begin-metadata-rebuild.md"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome: made unnecessary by #2030."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A first revision of this branch added a\ncanceled lane to the metadata composition oracle. An earlier held transaction\ndeleted key 1, the open transaction wrote against that projection, and the\nearlier one was canceled. The lane found that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" lost an explicit\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.row.set"},{"type":"text","value":" when the canceled delete turned the open insert into an\nidempotent re-insert, and the revision fixed the rebuild."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PR #2030 then allowed only the open last sync transaction to be canceled. Aborting\nan accepted transaction's signal now has no effect, so a rebuild can no longer\nreclassify an open write. The canceled lane's history no longer exists, and RB2\nis equivalent again. This branch drops the lane and the rebuild change and\nkeeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"'s rebuild."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-a-ready-callback-error-from-a-sync-entry-truncate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. A ready callback error from a sync-entry truncate"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gap."}]},{"type":"text","value":" During sync entry, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ops.markReady()"},{"type":"text","value":" deferred a ready callback's error\nuntil the sync function returned. A truncate committed inside the sync\nfunction threw the same error from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"},{"type":"text","value":". The rest of the sync function\nnever ran, and the Collection moved to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Witness."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The sync reentrancy oracle runs a throwing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFirstReady"},{"type":"text","value":" callback\nwith "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markReady"},{"type":"text","value":", a truncate commit, and a truncate commit followed by\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markReady"},{"type":"text","value":". The sync function must finish, the Collection must stay ready with\nits rows, and the error must surface when sync entry returns. The two truncate\ncases fail on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repair."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The lifecycle holds ready-effect failures while a sync function\nruns, whichever path makes the Collection ready, and sync entry reports the\nfirst one when it returns. This replaces "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markReadyDuringSyncStart"},{"type":"text","value":" and the\nper-entry flag that chose between two "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markReady"},{"type":"text","value":" calls."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-the-sync-commit-s-virtual-props-cache-delete","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. The sync commit's virtual props cache delete"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finding."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The round 3 record reported 422 reads that returned a cached\nenriched row whose fields differed from the stored row. Those came from\ncomparing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"!=="},{"type":"text","value":". With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.is"},{"type":"text","value":", instrumentation found no such\nread across the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" suite, with or without the delete."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome: kept."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A first revision removed the delete. A high-effort review\nthen showed that the suite runs only in development builds, where the\nreused-row check rejects an in-place change without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previousValue"},{"type":"text","value":". In a\nproduction build that write is accepted and publishes no update, so only the\ncommit's delete keeps reads fresh. A deferred publication also enriches late.\nNew cases in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"virtual-props-cache.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" stub production mode for that write\nand read inside a deferred publication. Both fail without the delete, so it\nstays."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-the-sync-commit-s-completed-optimistic-keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. The sync commit's completed optimistic keys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome: removed by #2030."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A first revision of this branch removed the set,\nand review then described a history where it might still matter, so the\nrevision restored it. #2030 drops optimistic state at settlement and removed\nthe set on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"review-of-this-record","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review of this record"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A high-effort review found nine items."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The cache delete still mattered in production builds. Reverted, with\nwitnesses that fail without it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Insert-shaped and deferred publications of a reused row read the cache\nlate. The deferred-publication witness covers the second; the delete covers\nboth."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A history may still need "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"completedOptimisticKeys"},{"type":"text","value":". Reverted, then\nremoved on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" by #2030."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A ready failure held during sync entry is dropped if the sync function then\nthrows. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ops.markReady()"},{"type":"text","value":" already behaves this way on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":", so the\ntruncate path now matches it. No change."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ready failure sink restored an outer sink that cannot exist. Removed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A cache comment described the removed delete. Resolved by the revert."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rebuild replay had a simpler equivalent form. Adopted, then dropped\nwith the rebuild change after #2030. The 2026-10-06 nested-begin fix\nrestores it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A hydration transaction rebuilt through a cancellation could lose its\nmetadata. #2030 marks hydration metadata as explicit, which fixes it on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first reused-row witness had no demonstrated kill. Replaced by the\nproduction and deferred cases."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The simplifier pass suggested one helper for the explicit metadata write,\nwhich "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.row.set"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.row.delete"},{"type":"text","value":" now share."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"orc-outcomes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC outcomes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-001: met."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Item 2 cites the deferred ready-failure contract of\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ops.markReady()"},{"type":"text","value":". Item 3 cites the reused-row contract: reads return a\nrow's current value. Items 1 and 4 change no code here."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-002: met."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The sync-entry and reused-row witnesses expect fixed\noutcomes and read no production state."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-003: met."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Each witness states its law beside its code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-004: not applicable."}]},{"type":"text","value":" No generated grammar changed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-005: met."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Each witness runs a real Collection through its sync API\nand observes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.status"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.state"},{"type":"text","value":", and public reads."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-006: met."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":" fails the two sync-entry truncate cases. Removing\nthe cache delete fails the production and deferred reused-row cases."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-007: not applicable."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The witnesses are fixed cases."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-008: not applicable."}]},{"type":"text","value":" No stateful model changed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-009: met."}]},{"type":"text","value":" \"Sync entry\" means the synchronous run of the sync\nfunction inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startSync"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-010: met."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Each witness cleans up its Collection in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finally"},{"type":"text","value":"\nblock."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-011: not applicable."}]},{"type":"text","value":" No reviewer named a shared fault."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-012: met by this record."}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-013: met."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The sync-entry witness keeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markReady"},{"type":"text","value":" as the control\ncase. The reused-row witnesses sit beside the existing cases that declare\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previousValue"},{"type":"text","value":" and publish at once."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-014: not applicable."}]},{"type":"text","value":" No controlled provider or host supplies a\npremise."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"state-mutation-round-3-follow-ups","text":"State mutation round 3 follow-ups","level":1},{"id":"1-metadata-rebuild-after-a-canceled-earlier-transaction","text":"1. Metadata rebuild after a canceled earlier transaction","level":2},{"id":"2-a-ready-callback-error-from-a-sync-entry-truncate","text":"2. A ready callback error from a sync-entry truncate","level":2},{"id":"3-the-sync-commit-s-virtual-props-cache-delete","text":"3. The sync commit's virtual props cache delete","level":2},{"id":"4-the-sync-commit-s-completed-optimistic-keys","text":"4. The sync commit's completed optimistic keys","level":2},{"id":"review-of-this-record","text":"Review of this record","level":2},{"id":"orc-outcomes","text":"ORC outcomes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# State mutation round 3 follow-ups\n\nBase revision: `cfb03f201` (`main` after #2032 and #2033).\n\nThis record closes the four items that the round 3 record and the\nready-callback truncate record left open. One is a bug fix. The cache delete\nstays, with witnesses. #2030 on `main` made the other two unnecessary.\n\n## 1. Metadata rebuild after a canceled earlier transaction\n\n**Gap.** The round 3 record called RB2, a mutant that keeps stale automatic\nmetadata writes through a rebuild, equivalent within legal histories. Reaching\nit needed a canceled earlier transaction, which the grammar did not generate.\n\n**Correction, 2026-10-06.** The outcome below is wrong. A transaction begun\ninside an open one can still commit first, and the rebuild then reclassifies\nthe open one's inserts. `main` loses last-write-wins there. See\n[`2026-10-06-nested-begin-metadata-rebuild.md`](2026-10-06-nested-begin-metadata-rebuild.md).\n\n**Outcome: made unnecessary by #2030.** A first revision of this branch added a\ncanceled lane to the metadata composition oracle. An earlier held transaction\ndeleted key 1, the open transaction wrote against that projection, and the\nearlier one was canceled. The lane found that `main` lost an explicit\n`metadata.row.set` when the canceled delete turned the open insert into an\nidempotent re-insert, and the revision fixed the rebuild.\n\nPR #2030 then allowed only the open last sync transaction to be canceled. Aborting\nan accepted transaction's signal now has no effect, so a rebuild can no longer\nreclassify an open write. The canceled lane's history no longer exists, and RB2\nis equivalent again. This branch drops the lane and the rebuild change and\nkeeps `main`'s rebuild.\n\n## 2. A ready callback error from a sync-entry truncate\n\n**Gap.** During sync entry, `ops.markReady()` deferred a ready callback's error\nuntil the sync function returned. A truncate committed inside the sync\nfunction threw the same error from `commit()`. The rest of the sync function\nnever ran, and the Collection moved to `error`.\n\n**Witness.** The sync reentrancy oracle runs a throwing `onFirstReady` callback\nwith `markReady`, a truncate commit, and a truncate commit followed by\n`markReady`. The sync function must finish, the Collection must stay ready with\nits rows, and the error must surface when sync entry returns. The two truncate\ncases fail on `main`.\n\n**Repair.** The lifecycle holds ready-effect failures while a sync function\nruns, whichever path makes the Collection ready, and sync entry reports the\nfirst one when it returns. This replaces `markReadyDuringSyncStart` and the\nper-entry flag that chose between two `markReady` calls.\n\n## 3. The sync commit's virtual props cache delete\n\n**Finding.** The round 3 record reported 422 reads that returned a cached\nenriched row whose fields differed from the stored row. Those came from\ncomparing `NaN` with `!==`. With `Object.is`, instrumentation found no such\nread across the `@tanstack/db` suite, with or without the delete.\n\n**Outcome: kept.** A first revision removed the delete. A high-effort review\nthen showed that the suite runs only in development builds, where the\nreused-row check rejects an in-place change without `previousValue`. In a\nproduction build that write is accepted and publishes no update, so only the\ncommit's delete keeps reads fresh. A deferred publication also enriches late.\nNew cases in `virtual-props-cache.test.ts` stub production mode for that write\nand read inside a deferred publication. Both fail without the delete, so it\nstays.\n\n## 4. The sync commit's completed optimistic keys\n\n**Outcome: removed by #2030.** A first revision of this branch removed the set,\nand review then described a history where it might still matter, so the\nrevision restored it. #2030 drops optimistic state at settlement and removed\nthe set on `main`.\n\n## Review of this record\n\nA high-effort review found nine items.\n\n1. The cache delete still mattered in production builds. Reverted, with\n   witnesses that fail without it.\n2. Insert-shaped and deferred publications of a reused row read the cache\n   late. The deferred-publication witness covers the second; the delete covers\n   both.\n3. A history may still need `completedOptimisticKeys`. Reverted, then\n   removed on `main` by #2030.\n4. A ready failure held during sync entry is dropped if the sync function then\n   throws. `ops.markReady()` already behaves this way on `main`, so the\n   truncate path now matches it. No change.\n5. The ready failure sink restored an outer sink that cannot exist. Removed.\n6. A cache comment described the removed delete. Resolved by the revert.\n7. The rebuild replay had a simpler equivalent form. Adopted, then dropped\n   with the rebuild change after #2030. The 2026-10-06 nested-begin fix\n   restores it.\n8. A hydration transaction rebuilt through a cancellation could lose its\n   metadata. #2030 marks hydration metadata as explicit, which fixes it on\n   `main`.\n9. The first reused-row witness had no demonstrated kill. Replaced by the\n   production and deferred cases.\n\nThe simplifier pass suggested one helper for the explicit metadata write,\nwhich `metadata.row.set` and `metadata.row.delete` now share.\n\n## ORC outcomes\n\n- **ORC-001: met.** Item 2 cites the deferred ready-failure contract of\n  `ops.markReady()`. Item 3 cites the reused-row contract: reads return a\n  row's current value. Items 1 and 4 change no code here.\n- **ORC-002: met.** The sync-entry and reused-row witnesses expect fixed\n  outcomes and read no production state.\n- **ORC-003: met.** Each witness states its law beside its code.\n- **ORC-004: not applicable.** No generated grammar changed.\n- **ORC-005: met.** Each witness runs a real Collection through its sync API\n  and observes `collection.status`, `collection.state`, and public reads.\n- **ORC-006: met.** `main` fails the two sync-entry truncate cases. Removing\n  the cache delete fails the production and deferred reused-row cases.\n- **ORC-007: not applicable.** The witnesses are fixed cases.\n- **ORC-008: not applicable.** No stateful model changed.\n- **ORC-009: met.** \"Sync entry\" means the synchronous run of the sync\n  function inside `startSync`.\n- **ORC-010: met.** Each witness cleans up its Collection in a `finally`\n  block.\n- **ORC-011: not applicable.** No reviewer named a shared fault.\n- **ORC-012: met by this record.**\n- **ORC-013: met.** The sync-entry witness keeps `markReady` as the control\n  case. The reused-row witnesses sit beside the existing cases that declare\n  `previousValue` and publish at once.\n- **ORC-014: not applicable.** No controlled provider or host supplies a\n  premise.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# State mutation round 3 follow-ups\n\nBase revision: `cfb03f201` (`main` after #2032 and #2033).\n\nThis record closes the four items that the round 3 record and the\nready-callback truncate record left open. One is a bug fix. The cache delete\nstays, with witnesses. #2030 on `main` made the other two unnecessary.\n\n## 1. Metadata rebuild after a canceled earlier transaction\n\n**Gap.** The round 3 record called RB2, a mutant that keeps stale automatic\nmetadata writes through a rebuild, equivalent within legal histories. Reaching\nit needed a canceled earlier transaction, which the grammar did not generate.\n\n**Correction, 2026-10-06.** The outcome below is wrong. A transaction begun\ninside an open one can still commit first, and the rebuild then reclassifies\nthe open one's inserts. `main` loses last-write-wins there. See\n[`2026-10-06-nested-begin-metadata-rebuild.md`](2026-10-06-nested-begin-metadata-rebuild.md).\n\n**Outcome: made unnecessary by #2030.** A first revision of this branch added a\ncanceled lane to the metadata composition oracle. An earlier held transaction\ndeleted key 1, the open transaction wrote against that projection, and the\nearlier one was canceled. The lane found that `main` lost an explicit\n`metadata.row.set` when the canceled delete turned the open insert into an\nidempotent re-insert, and the revision fixed the rebuild.\n\nPR #2030 then allowed only the open last sync transaction to be canceled. Aborting\nan accepted transaction's signal now has no effect, so a rebuild can no longer\nreclassify an open write. The canceled lane's history no longer exists, and RB2\nis equivalent again. This branch drops the lane and the rebuild change and\nkeeps `main`'s rebuild.\n\n## 2. A ready callback error from a sync-entry truncate\n\n**Gap.** During sync entry, `ops.markReady()` deferred a ready callback's error\nuntil the sync function returned. A truncate committed inside the sync\nfunction threw the same error from `commit()`. The rest of the sync function\nnever ran, and the Collection moved to `error`.\n\n**Witness.** The sync reentrancy oracle runs a throwing `onFirstReady` callback\nwith `markReady`, a truncate commit, and a truncate commit followed by\n`markReady`. The sync function must finish, the Collection must stay ready with\nits rows, and the error must surface when sync entry returns. The two truncate\ncases fail on `main`.\n\n**Repair.** The lifecycle holds ready-effect failures while a sync function\nruns, whichever path makes the Collection ready, and sync entry reports the\nfirst one when it returns. This replaces `markReadyDuringSyncStart` and the\nper-entry flag that chose between two `markReady` calls.\n\n## 3. The sync commit's virtual props cache delete\n\n**Finding.** The round 3 record reported 422 reads that returned a cached\nenriched row whose fields differed from the stored row. Those came from\ncomparing `NaN` with `!==`. With `Object.is`, instrumentation found no such\nread across the `@tanstack/db` suite, with or without the delete.\n\n**Outcome: kept.** A first revision removed the delete. A high-effort review\nthen showed that the suite runs only in development builds, where the\nreused-row check rejects an in-place change without `previousValue`. In a\nproduction build that write is accepted and publishes no update, so only the\ncommit's delete keeps reads fresh. A deferred publication also enriches late.\nNew cases in `virtual-props-cache.test.ts` stub production mode for that write\nand read inside a deferred publication. Both fail without the delete, so it\nstays.\n\n## 4. The sync commit's completed optimistic keys\n\n**Outcome: removed by #2030.** A first revision of this branch removed the set,\nand review then described a history where it might still matter, so the\nrevision restored it. #2030 drops optimistic state at settlement and removed\nthe set on `main`.\n\n## Review of this record\n\nA high-effort review found nine items.\n\n1. The cache delete still mattered in production builds. Reverted, with\n   witnesses that fail without it.\n2. Insert-shaped and deferred publications of a reused row read the cache\n   late. The deferred-publication witness covers the second; the delete covers\n   both.\n3. A history may still need `completedOptimisticKeys`. Reverted, then\n   removed on `main` by #2030.\n4. A ready failure held during sync entry is dropped if the sync function then\n   throws. `ops.markReady()` already behaves this way on `main`, so the\n   truncate path now matches it. No change.\n5. The ready failure sink restored an outer sink that cannot exist. Removed.\n6. A cache comment described the removed delete. Resolved by the revert.\n7. The rebuild replay had a simpler equivalent form. Adopted, then dropped\n   with the rebuild change after #2030. The 2026-10-06 nested-begin fix\n   restores it.\n8. A hydration transaction rebuilt through a cancellation could lose its\n   metadata. #2030 marks hydration metadata as explicit, which fixes it on\n   `main`.\n9. The first reused-row witness had no demonstrated kill. Replaced by the\n   production and deferred cases.\n\nThe simplifier pass suggested one helper for the explicit metadata write,\nwhich `metadata.row.set` and `metadata.row.delete` now share.\n\n## ORC outcomes\n\n- **ORC-001: met.** Item 2 cites the deferred ready-failure contract of\n  `ops.markReady()`. Item 3 cites the reused-row contract: reads return a\n  row's current value. Items 1 and 4 change no code here.\n- **ORC-002: met.** The sync-entry and reused-row witnesses expect fixed\n  outcomes and read no production state.\n- **ORC-003: met.** Each witness states its law beside its code.\n- **ORC-004: not applicable.** No generated grammar changed.\n- **ORC-005: met.** Each witness runs a real Collection through its sync API\n  and observes `collection.status`, `collection.state`, and public reads.\n- **ORC-006: met.** `main` fails the two sync-entry truncate cases. Removing\n  the cache delete fails the production and deferred reused-row cases.\n- **ORC-007: not applicable.** The witnesses are fixed cases.\n- **ORC-008: not applicable.** No stateful model changed.\n- **ORC-009: met.** \"Sync entry\" means the synchronous run of the sync\n  function inside `startSync`.\n- **ORC-010: met.** Each witness cleans up its Collection in a `finally`\n  block.\n- **ORC-011: not applicable.** No reviewer named a shared fault.\n- **ORC-012: met by this record.**\n- **ORC-013: met.** The sync-entry witness keeps `markReady` as the control\n  case. The reused-row witnesses sit beside the existing cases that declare\n  `previousValue` and publish at once.\n- **ORC-014: not applicable.** No controlled provider or host supplies a\n  premise.\n"}
